; =========================================================================================
; DISCOVERIES & ANALYSIS
; =========================================================================================
; Game Identity: BattleTech: The Crescent Hawk's Inception (1988)
; Original File: UNBTECH.exe (likely BTECH.EXE unpacked)
; Platform: MS-DOS 16-bit Real Mode (MZ Executable)
; Compiler: Microsoft C 5.0 (detected by Reko)
;
; SEGMENT ANALYSIS:
; -----------------
; Code Segments:
; - 0x0800: Core Logic / Main Library
; - 0x183B: Graphics & UI Initialization (VGA/EGA Ports 0x3C8, 0x3DA)
; - 0x204B: Timer (INT 8) & Sound (PC Speaker Port 0x61, 0x43)
; - 0x207F: Utility / Helper Functions
;
; GRAPHICS & RESOURCES:
; ---------------------
; - Graphics are likely stored in external files (referenced in strings):
;   TRAINING.BLD, CITADEL.BLD, STARLEAG.ICN, ENDMECH.CMP, etc.
; - The EXE handles loading and rendering these resources.
; - Video Mode: Likely VGA (Mode 13h) or EGA, using direct port I/O.
;
; GAMEPLAY LOGIC IDENTIFIED:
; --------------------------
; - 'Mech Combat: "Use Weapons", "Scan Unit", "Kick", "Heat Sink".
; - RPG Elements: Skills (Pistols, Rifles), Training.
; - Economy: Stock Market (Defiance, Nashan, Baker).
; - Map: "The computer is currently moving this unit".
;
; RECREATION STRATEGY:
; --------------------
; The Java recreation will implement a prototype focusing on:
; 1. Turn-based Combat System (Mechs, Weapons, Heat).
; 2. Stock Market Simulation.
; 3. Basic RPG Stats.
; Note: Original graphics assets are external/missing, placeholders will be used.
; =========================================================================================

